spans.s:
√kṣip (kṣipáti, -te; cikṣépa, cikṣipé;
kṣepsyáti, -te; kṣiptá; kṣéptum; kṣiptvā́;
-kṣípya; kṣepáyati). dart; cast;
throw, caus. cause to fly or burst, 84^4.
+ ā,
 —1. throw at;
 —2. fig. (like Eng.
fling, make flings at), deride, put to shame,
8^10;
 —3. draw towards one's self, call out
(a person to vindicate himself), 55^6.
+ ni, throw down (one's self, one's body).
+ vi-ni, lay down separately or orderly.
+ sam, dash together in a heap; destroy.
